+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P0] Studio CI green: fix the 2 gesture-test failures (jsdom lacks PointerEvent → clientY undefined → dy NaN)
+
+Addresses `handoff:coder` CI-failure order on `Supremeai-bd/supremeai-studio` main
+(#1492 — Run 40485128169; siblings #1489 run 40481462890, #1488 run 40481410235 — one
+shared root cause). Failures started with the iOS Home Launcher part-2/3 sync
+(#1485, commit d6407bd): every run dies at the Test step (2 failed / 668 passed), so
+"Deploy to Cloudflare Pages" is skipped and production has been stale since 2026-10-27.
+
+## Root cause (reproduced locally, exact)
+`src/components/mobile/HomeShell.test.tsx` fires `fireEvent.pointerDown/Up` with
+`{ clientY: N }` for the status-bar pull-down and bottom-strip pull-up gestures.
+This jsdom version has **no `window.PointerEvent`** (verified: `typeof window.PointerEvent === 'undefined'`),
+so @testing-library falls back to a plain `Event` and **drops the `clientY` init**
+(React handler observes `e.clientY === undefined`). Gesture math then computes
+`dy = e.clientY - startY = NaN`, both guards (`dy > 28`, `Math.abs(dy) < 6`, `dy > -6`)
+evaluate false on NaN, `setPanel` never runs, panel stays `'none'`, and
+`getByTestId('notification-center')` / `getByTestId('control-center')` fail:
+- `HomeShell.test.tsx:77` — "pull-down on status bar opens Notification Center with Clear"
+- `HomeShell.test.tsx:87` — "bottom strip opens Control Center and toggles Wi-Fi"
+
+The production components are correct: in every real browser `PointerEvent` carries
+`clientY`. This is purely a test-environment gap — the same class of gap the test file
+already handles for `ResizeObserver`, `matchMedia`, and `clientWidth/Height` stubs
+(documented in its own header comment), which simply missed `PointerEvent`.
+
+## The fix (1 file, +7 lines, test-only, zero production change)
+- **studio/src/components/mobile/HomeShell.test.tsx**: extend the existing jsdom-stub
+  block with `class PointerEventStub extends MouseEvent {}` +
+  `vi.stubGlobal('PointerEvent', PointerEventStub)` and a Bangla comment explaining why.
+  With the shim, `fireEvent` constructs real MouseEvent-derived events and `clientY`
+  survives → gestures behave exactly as in a browser.
+
+## Verification (real, local, reproducible)
+- BEFORE (clean clone of 31e6330, pnpm 9.15.9, Node 24): `vitest run` → 2 failed | 668 passed;
+  debug probe printed `PANEL_AFTER_STATUSBAR_PULL= none`, `PANEL_AFTER_STRIP_PULL= none`.
+- Pointer probe: without shim `clientY=undefined`; with shim `down=10, up=60`.
+- AFTER: `pnpm run test` → **124 files, 670/670 passed**; `pnpm run typecheck` clean;
+  `pnpm run lint` → 0 errors (146 pre-existing warnings, unchanged); `pnpm run build` →
+  ✓ built in 7.5s; `eslint src/components/mobile/HomeShell.test.tsx` → clean.
+- U9 sibling sweep: grep of all `fireEvent.pointer*` usages — only `RunsPage.test.tsx`
+  (fires pointerDown with no clientY; handler reads only `transitionEnd`, unaffected).
+  No other sibling defects → no follow-up issue needed.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P0-critical` `area:ci` `repo:studio` `handoff:coder`
